            <ArticleTitle>Thrombus formation after aortic valvular replacement using Björk-Shiley valve occluding the right coronary orifice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>99-100</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a patient with unstable angina due to occlusion of the orifice of the right coronary artery by thrombus formation after aortic valvular replacement using a Björk-Shiley valve. After strict anticoagulant treatment, transesophageal echocardiography demonstrated disappearance of the thrombus formation around the orifice of the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
